course: dictionary
lesson: 12648
title: Displeasure and feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Displeasure is a noun. It means the feeling you have when you are annoyed or not satisfied with someone or something. It is a rather formal word, so you will meet it mostly in stories and news, not in everyday chat.
explain: You can show displeasure without saying a word. «Mum gave a deep sigh when she saw the muddy footprints on the clean floor.» The sigh is the clue: she is not happy about the mess, so the sigh shows her displeasure.
explain: Look out for the common phrases: «show displeasure», «express displeasure», and «to someone's displeasure». Displeasure is uncountable, so we never say «a displeasure» or «displeasures».
fact: Displeasure means a feeling of being annoyed or not satisfied.
fact: Displeasure is uncountable: you say «her displeasure», not «a displeasure».
fact: «Show displeasure» means let others see that you are annoyed, for example by frowning or sighing.
fact: «Incur someone's displeasure» means to make someone annoyed with you.
fact: You can understand a text well without knowing every word; skip, read on, then come back.
exercise: «Mum gave a deep sigh of displeasure when she saw the muddy footprints.» What does displeasure mean here? | *Feeling annoyed about the mess | Feeling very happy and proud | Feeling cold on a winter day | Feeling sleepy after lunch
exercise: What did the teacher do to show her displeasure? «The teacher showed her displeasure by frowning at the noisy class.» | She sang a song | She gave out prizes | *She frowned | She ran out of the room
exercise: Which sentence uses displeasure correctly, because displeasure is uncountable? | She had a displeasure about the rain | Two displeasures came into the room | *Her displeasure was clear to everyone | Her displeasures were clear to everyone
test: «The manager sent a letter of complaint, expressing his displeasure with the late delivery.» How is the manager feeling? | Tired after a long walk | Hungry for his lunch | *Annoyed that the delivery was late | Pleased with the delivery
test: Which word means nearly the same as displeasure? | Sleep | *Annoyance | Calm | Joy
exam: «To the referee's displeasure, the players kept arguing instead of playing.» Why did the referee feel displeasure? | The referee had won a prize | The players were winning the match | *The players were arguing instead of playing | The players had all gone home
